{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Moses made a serpent of bronze</b> – He was not told to make it of bronze, but Moses reasoned: the Holy One, blessed be He, said to me \"serpent\" [נָחָשׁ], so I will make it of bronze [נְחֹשֶׁת] — a play on words. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 21:9) from the words of our Sages (Genesis Rabbah 31:8). But I do not understand this, for the Holy One, blessed be He, did not say to him \"serpent\" but rather \"Make yourself a seraph\" [שָׂרָף]. Rather, their opinion is that Moses followed the name of the creature that was upon it. And what seems right in my eyes regarding the secret of this matter is that it is from the ways of the Torah, that all its deeds are a miracle within a miracle: you remove the harm through that which harms, and you heal the illness through that which sickens, as they mentioned (Mekhilta, VaYissa 1) regarding \"and YHWH showed him a tree\" (Exodus 15:25), and so too with the salt of Elisha in the water (II Kings 2:21). It is known from the ways of medicine that all who are bitten by creatures of venom are endangered by seeing them or by seeing their image — to the extent that those bitten by a rabid dog, and likewise other rabid animals, if they look into water, the image of the dog or the harmful creature will appear to them there and they will die, as is written in the books of medicine and is mentioned in the Gemara in tractate Yoma (Yoma 84a). And so the physicians guard against mentioning the name of the biting creature in their presence, that they should not mention it at all, for their soul would cleave to that thought and would not separate from it at all until it kills them. And they already mentioned a tested matter from the wonders of nature, that the bite of a rabid dog after it has gone mad in its illness — if its urine is received in a glass vessel, one will see in the urine the image of tiny dog pups, and if you pass the water through a cloth and strain them, you will not find in them any trace at all, and when you return them to the glass vessel and they sit there for an hour, you will again see there the dog pups clearly — and this is a true thing among the wonders of the soul's powers. And when all this is so, it would have been proper for Israel, those bitten by the seraph serpents, not to see a serpent and not to remember one and not to bring it to mind at all; yet the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded Moses to make for them an image of a seraph — that is, the very thing that kills them. And it is known that the seraph serpents are red-eyed, broad-headed, their bodies like the color of bronze on their necks, and therefore Moses found no way to fulfill his command to make a seraph other than by making a serpent of bronze, for that is the image of a seraph serpent, and if he made it from another material it would be the image of a serpent but not the image of a seraph. And what they said about the wordplay — that the mention of the name alone causes harm. The principle is that HaShem commanded that they be healed through the very harmful thing that kills by nature, and they made its image and its name, and when a person would gaze with intention at the bronze serpent, which is entirely like the harmful creature, he would live — to make known to them that HaShem kills and brings to life."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:33.373523531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}